    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "873ec04cb555c8dd6bf9016dcd7e1c33",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"what-hope-scores\">What HOPE scores</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For a BatchNorm output modeled as <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(z=\\beta+|\\gamma|X||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X\\sim\\mathcal N(0,1)||)</marimo-tex>,\nthe squared Hilbert norm after ReLU is</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nK=(\\gamma^2+\\beta^2)\\Phi(\\beta/|\\gamma|)\n  +\\beta|\\gamma|\\phi(\\beta/|\\gamma|).\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">Multiplying <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\sqrt K||)</marimo-tex> by the outgoing weight norm gives neuron capacity. The\ndistortion-rate score divides the paper's pruning penalty by the channel's static\nfootprint. We implemented that score, input-weight L1, joint input/output L1, and\nBatchNorm-scale baselines over internal residual-block channels.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
