    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "5260dd79508401d8e5297b97dadaaa0d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"numerical-and-scope-checks\">Numerical and scope checks</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Across five fresh model/seed conditions, the analytic kernel's median relative error\nagainst 100,000-sample Monte Carlo estimates was <strong>0.61\u20130.84%</strong> (64 channels each).\nThe experiment used post-BatchNorm masks equivalent to deleting selected internal\nchannels and downstream input slices. It used no fine-tuning, recalibration, merging,\nblock eviction, or DEFT.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Compute: Kubernetes, peak 16 concurrent <strong>NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell</strong> GPUs,\n0.42 hours measured experiment wall span. See the linked report and source repository\nfor branch-level provenance and the exact fixed run command.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
